1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,560
Today I am going to show you the eighth wonder of the world:

2
00:00:06,560 --> 00:00:12,406
How to prepare a brownie, in five minutes, in a mug.

3
00:00:12,880 --> 00:00:16,640
We need a mug,

4
00:00:16,640 --> 00:00:24,800
and two spoons: a large spoon and a small spoon-

5
00:00:24,800 --> 00:00:28,379
See? This is the little girl, the daughter:

6
00:00:28,379 --> 00:00:33,148
Mom, Mom! Daughter!

7
00:00:33,750 --> 00:00:37,920
Ingredients: flour, oil,

8
00:00:37,920 --> 00:00:44,960
this is olive oil, but any oil works:

9
00:00:44,960 --> 00:00:47,849
it can be coconut or sunflower oil.

10
00:00:47,849 --> 00:00:50,594
But I have olive.

11
00:00:50,594 --> 00:00:52,393
Water.

12
00:00:52,393 --> 00:00:56,855
Salt.

13
00:00:58,112 --> 00:00:59,660
Sal.

14
00:00:59,660 --> 00:01:01,920
Get out of here! ...No.

15
00:01:01,920 --> 00:01:05,129
And cocoa powder.

16
00:01:05,129 --> 00:01:08,480
Cocoa, chocolate: powder.

17
00:01:08,480 --> 00:01:11,330
This is ... this is cocoa.

18
00:01:11,330 --> 00:01:18,017
In fact it is colacao, because I do not have pure cocoa.

19
00:01:18,017 --> 00:01:25,770
Colacao is a brand to make chocolate milk in Spain.

20
00:01:25,770 --> 00:01:26,940
It's my favorite.

21
00:01:26,940 --> 00:01:33,280
We are going to take all the measures with a large spoon:

22
00:01:33,280 --> 00:01:38,296
We start with the dry ingredients, that is:

23
00:01:38,296 --> 00:01:45,000
The flour, the sugar, the cocoa powder and the salt.

24
00:01:45,380 --> 00:01:52,320
When you take the measurements, they have to be flat, okay?

25
00:01:52,320 --> 00:01:57,151
This is level: it has to be flat.

26
00:01:57,151 --> 00:02:01,280
It can't be a mountain of flour.

27
00:02:02,490 --> 00:02:08,114
This cannot be, this is not leveled.

28
00:02:12,965 --> 00:02:15,035
Brown sugar:

29
00:02:16,920 --> 00:02:20,924
Also 4 leveled tablespoons.

30
00:02:24,270 --> 00:02:25,327
This is not leveled-

31
00:02:30,030 --> 00:02:33,920
I've spread it everywhere ...

32
00:02:34,223 --> 00:02:37,181
Now cocoa:

33
00:02:38,620 --> 00:02:43,360
Two leveled tablespoons

34
00:02:44,720 --> 00:02:47,360
A pinch of salt.

35
00:02:47,360 --> 00:02:50,660
Salt is very important, very important.

36
00:02:50,660 --> 00:02:56,320
Don't forget, you have to put a little bit of salt.

37
00:02:56,320 --> 00:03:00,000
And now we mix it up.

38
00:03:02,100 --> 00:03:08,160
We mix it well and once it is very well mixed,

39
00:03:08,160 --> 00:03:10,578
we add the water ...

40
00:03:13,130 --> 00:03:14,699
Two tablespoons.

41
00:03:16,480 --> 00:03:18,560
And the oil.

42
00:03:21,210 --> 00:03:23,850
Oops ... just there, just there, just there.

43
00:03:23,850 --> 00:03:25,530
We mix it again.

44
00:03:30,380 --> 00:03:38,080
Okay, and the texture has to be something like this.

45
00:03:38,080 --> 00:03:41,645
When you have this texture,

46
00:03:41,920 --> 00:03:48,012
it's ready to go into the microwave.

47
00:03:48,012 --> 00:03:55,136
Depending on the power, if it is a very strong microwave, you put less time.

48
00:03:55,136 --> 00:04:02,876
If it's a weaker microwave, you put it more time.

49
00:04:02,876 --> 00:04:11,724
And you have to put it around 1 minute: 1 minute and 10 seconds or 50 seconds ...

50
00:04:11,724 --> 00:04:15,688
That's where the time range is.

51
00:04:29,025 --> 00:04:31,520
Ah! It burns, it burns, it burns, it burns!

52
00:04:31,520 --> 00:04:37,280
Be careful because it burns a lot when it comes out of the microwave.

53
00:04:37,280 --> 00:04:44,160
The brownie has a pretty good texture, look:

54
00:04:47,970 --> 00:04:56,640
This is a recipe that I prepare when I am very hungry and I want chocolate,

55
00:04:56,640 --> 00:05:01,296
but I do not have much time.

56
00:05:01,296 --> 00:05:08,193
So with 5 minutes, these ingredients, and a microwave,

57
00:05:08,193 --> 00:05:12,480
you can make a delicious brownie.

58
00:05:12,480 --> 00:05:16,407
I leave the recipe here,

59
00:05:16,407 --> 00:05:23,310
and if you also make it, tell me in a comment.

60
00:05:23,310 --> 00:05:28,781
Say: Hey Laura! I made myself a brownie too!

61
00:05:28,781 --> 00:05:32,476
And you tell me if you liked it or not.

62
00:05:32,476 --> 00:05:34,720
If you did not like it at all.

63
00:05:34,720 --> 00:05:39,840
For more Spanish, don't forget to subscribe.

64
00:05:39,840 --> 00:05:43,620
And see you next week-

65
00:05:43,620 --> 00:05:45,000
Bye!